 "title": "Saccharomyces cerevisiae and bPACy Metabolomics Analysis",
 "summary": "This cluster revolves around the organisms Saccharomyces cerevisiae and bPACy, which are involved in metabolomics analysis. Saccharomyces cerevisiae uses methods such as Genomics and metabolomics, while bPACy has lower adenylate energy charge and is exposed to darkness. The organisms are also inoculated with LFM and have plasmids. The metabolome of both organisms is related to WT, and bPACy has β-carotene. cAMP regulates several genes and proteins, including PKA, Pde1, and adenylate cyclase, and increases the production of β-carotene and Cordycepin.",
